from the article to the comment. Pairing the positive check with an explicit refusal of that value is what stops a lazy run scoring on a lenient lookup.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"xlsx\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"metrics.xlsx\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?im)^[^\\\\S\\\\n]*(?:\\\\|[^\\\\S\\\\n]*)*[*_`\\\\\\\"']{0,2}articles[ _-]without[ _-]comments[*_`\\\\\\\"']{0,2}[^\\\\S\\\\n]*(?:\\\\|[^\\\\S\\\\n]*)+[*_`\\\\\\\"']{0,2}7(?:\\\\.0+)?(?!\\\\d)\",\n              \"deterministic\": {\n                \"path\": \"$.text\",\n                \"comparison\": \"not_regex_match\"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"review_log_lists_every_reviewer_comment\",\n      \"description\": \"review_log.md carries exactly one line per reviewer comment (19 of them, each ending in its thread's finding) and names the four articles that carry none, so all 18 articles appear in the file.\",\n      \"category\": \"core\",\n      \"weight\": 1.0,\n      \"target\": \"workspace_files\",\n      \"verifier_type\": \"file_check\",\n      \"type\": \"file_check\",\n      \"pass_threshold\": 1.0,\n      \"requirement_id\": \"review_log_row_coverage\",\n      \"evidence_span\": \"One line for every reviewer comment in that database,\\nwritten as `article title | Doc stage | open` while the thread that comment belongs to is still\\nwaiting on somebody, and `article title | Doc stage | settled` once that thread has been resolved.\\nClose the file with a clearly labelled list, one title per line, of the articles carrying no\\nreviewer comment at all, so that every article in the database appears somewhere in this file.\",\n      \"metadata\": {\n        \"why_justification\": \"A run that writes one line per ARTICLE instead of one per comment lands on 14 lines, and a run that leaves include_resolved at its default never sees the four settled comments and lands on 15; both fail the count. A run that lists the four uncommented articles as log lines instead of naming them at the end lands on 23 and is refused twice over.\"\n      },\n      \"verifier_spec\": {\n        \"task_id\": \"review_log_lists_every_reviewer_comment\",\n        \"verifiers\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"review_log_has_one_line_per_comment\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"how_justification\": \"Reads review_log.md as text and requires EXACTLY 19 lines whose last pipe-separated field is open or settled - the shape the prompt asks each comment line to take. The pattern is an exact-count construction (n matches of the line pattern and nothing between them that also matches), not a floor, so 18 lines and 20 lines both fail. Everything before the last separator is free text, so the article title and the Doc stage may be written any way the run likes; leading and trailing pipes, markdown emphasis inside or around the status word, tabs, CRLF line endings and any casing all pass, and a heading or a table rule, having no status field, is not counted.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"A run that writes one line per ARTICLE instead of one per comment lands on 14 lines, and a run that leaves include_resolved at its default never sees the four settled comments and lands on 15; both fail the count. A run that lists the four uncommented articles as log lines instead of naming them at the end lands on 23 and is refused twice over.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"md\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"review_log.md\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?ism)\\\\A(?:(?!^[^\\\\r\\\\n]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*(?:[*_`]{0,2}(?:open|ope[*_`]{0,2}n)[*_`]{0,2}|[*_`]{0,2}(?:settled|set[*_`]{0,2}tled)[*_`]{0,2})[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$)[\\\\s\\\\S])*(?:(?:^[^\\\\r\\\\n]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*(?:[*_`]{0,2}(?:open|ope[*_`]{0,2}n)[*_`]{0,2}|[*_`]{0,2}(?:settled|set[*_`]{0,2}tled)[*_`]{0,2})[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$)(?:(?!^[^\\\\r\\\\n]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*(?:[*_`]{0,2}(?:open|ope[*_`]{0,2}n)[*_`]{0,2}|[*_`]{0,2}(?:settled|set[*_`]{0,2}tled)[*_`]{0,2})[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$)[\\\\s\\\\S])*){19}\\\\Z\",\n              \"deterministic\": {\n                \"path\": \"$.text\",\n                \"comparison\": \"regex_match\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"review_log_names_article_as_uncommented\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"how_justification\": \"Requires Article, which carries no reviewer comment, to appear on a line of its own - a line holding that title and nothing else - which is the closing list the prompt asks for. The line may be bare or carry any ordinary Markdown list marker ('-', '*', '+', '1.' or '1)'), and it may also be a single-cell table row ('| Article |'); a GFM header row, which is the row the delimiter line follows, is not a list entry and does not satisfy it. Markdown emphasis around or inside the words, any casing, tabs, CRLF and any position in the file pass; the title appearing only inside a heading or inside a comment line does not.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"Without a line of its own for each of the four, the file could cover the 14 articles that were commented on and silently drop the ones that were not, which is the half of the audit the summary figure articles_without_comments reports.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"md\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"review_log.md\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?im)(?:^[ \\\\t]*(?:[-*+][ \\\\t]*|[0-9]{1,9}[.)][ \\\\t]*)?[*_`]{0,2}(?:Article|Art[*_`]{0,2}icle)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}(?:Article|Art[*_`]{0,2}icle)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$(?!\\\\r?\\\\n[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*:?-))\",\n              \"deterministic\": {\n                \"path\": \"$.text\",\n                \"comparison\": \"regex_match\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"review_log_names_exercise_with_bump_as_uncommented\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"how_justification\": \"Requires Exercise with bump, which carries no reviewer comment, to appear on a line of its own - a line holding that title and nothing else - which is the closing list the prompt asks for. The line may be bare or carry any ordinary Markdown list marker ('-', '*', '+', '1.' or '1)'), and it may also be a single-cell table row ('| Exercise with bump |'); a GFM header row, which is the row the delimiter line follows, is not a list entry and does not satisfy it. Markdown emphasis around or inside the words, any casing, tabs, CRLF and any position in the file pass; the title appearing only inside a heading or inside a comment line does not.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"Without a line of its own for each of the four, the file could cover the 14 articles that were commented on and silently drop the ones that were not, which is the half of the audit the summary figure articles_without_comments reports.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"md\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"review_log.md\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?im)(?:^[ \\\\t]*(?:[-*+][ \\\\t]*|[0-9]{1,9}[.)][ \\\\t]*)?[*_`]{0,2}(?:Exercise|Exe[*_`]{0,2}rcise)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:with|wit[*_`]{0,2}h)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:bump|bum[*_`]{0,2}p)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}(?:Exercise|Exe[*_`]{0,2}rcise)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:with|wit[*_`]{0,2}h)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:bump|bum[*_`]{0,2}p)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$(?!\\\\r?\\\\n[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*:?-))\",\n              \"deterministic\": {\n                \"path\": \"$.text\",\n                \"comparison\": \"regex_match\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"review_log_names_new_brainstorm_as_uncommented\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"how_justification\": \"Requires New Brainstorm, which carries no reviewer comment, to appear on a line of its own - a line holding that title and nothing else - which is the closing list the prompt asks for. The line may be bare or carry any ordinary Markdown list marker ('-', '*', '+', '1.' or '1)'), and it may also be a single-cell table row ('| New Brainstorm |'); a GFM header row, which is the row the delimiter line follows, is not a list entry and does not satisfy it. Markdown emphasis around or inside the words, any casing, tabs, CRLF and any position in the file pass; the title appearing only inside a heading or inside a comment line does not.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"Without a line of its own for each of the four, the file could cover the 14 articles that were commented on and silently drop the ones that were not, which is the half of the audit the summary figure articles_without_comments reports.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"md\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"review_log.md\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?im)(?:^[ \\\\t]*(?:[-*+][ \\\\t]*|[0-9]{1,9}[.)][ \\\\t]*)?[*_`]{0,2}New[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Brainstorm|Bra[*_`]{0,2}instorm)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}New[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Brainstorm|Bra[*_`]{0,2}instorm)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$(?!\\\\r?\\\\n[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*:?-))\",\n              \"deterministic\": {\n                \"path\": \"$.text\",\n                \"comparison\": \"regex_match\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"review_log_names_new_product_spec_prd_as_uncommented\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"how_justification\": \"Requires New Product Spec (PRD), which carries no reviewer comment, to appear on a line of its own - a line holding that title and nothing else - which is the closing list the prompt asks for. The line may be bare or carry any ordinary Markdown list marker ('-', '*', '+', '1.' or '1)'), and it may also be a single-cell table row ('| New Product Spec (PRD) |'); a GFM header row, which is the row the delimiter line follows, is not a list entry and does not satisfy it. Markdown emphasis around or inside the words, any casing, tabs, CRLF and any position in the file pass; the title appearing only inside a heading or inside a comment line does not.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"Without a line of its own for each of the four, the file could cover the 14 articles that were commented on and silently drop the ones that were not, which is the half of the audit the summary figure articles_without_comments reports.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"md\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"review_log.md\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?im)(?:^[ \\\\t]*(?:[-*+][ \\\\t]*|[0-9]{1,9}[.)][ \\\\t]*)?[*_`]{0,2}New[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Product|Pro[*_`]{0,2}duct)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Spec|Spe[*_`]{0,2}c)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:\\\\(PRD\\\\)|\\\\(PR[*_`]{0,2}D\\\\))[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}New[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Product|Pro[*_`]{0,2}duct)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Spec|Spe[*_`]{0,2}c)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:\\\\(PRD\\\\)|\\\\(PR[*_`]{0,2}D\\\\))[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$(?!\\\\r?\\\\n[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*:?-))\",\n              \"deterministic\": {\n                \"path\": \"$.text\",\n                \"comparison\": \"regex_match\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          {\n            \"name\": \"review_log_refuses_a_comment_line_for_an_uncommented_article\",\n            \"metadata\": {\n              \"how_justification\": \"The paired refusal: none of those four titles may carry a COMMENT line - a line whose last pipe-separated field is the finding, open or settled - since they carry no comment for such a line to describe. It is the exact mirror of review_log_refuses_an_open_line_for_a_settled_article and of review_log_refuses_a_settled_line_for_a_still_open_article: the same title sub-patterns, the same optional outer pipes, the same free-text Doc stage field between the separators, the same emphasis, casing, tab and CRLF tolerance, and the same requirement that the line END in the finding. A GFM header row whose title column is spelled 'Article' carries a column name in its last field, not a finding, so rendering the log as a table is not refused; only a manufactured comment line is.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"A run that manufactures a placeholder row for an article with no comments would satisfy a membership check while corrupting both the row count and articles_without_comments.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",\n              \"file\": {\n                \"type\": \"md\",\n                \"command\": \"extract_text\",\n                \"arguments\": {\n                  \"path\": \"review_log.md\"\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            \"assertion\": {\n              \"type\": \"deterministic\",\n              \"expected\": \"(?im)(?:^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}(?:Article|Art[*_`]{0,2}icle)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[^|\\\\r\\\\n]*[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*(?:[*_`]{0,2}(?:open|ope[*_`]{0,2}n)[*_`]{0,2}|[*_`]{0,2}(?:settled|set[*_`]{0,2}tled)[*_`]{0,2})[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}(?:Exercise|Exe[*_`]{0,2}rcise)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:with|wit[*_`]{0,2}h)[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:bump|bum[*_`]{0,2}p)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[^|\\\\r\\\\n]*[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*(?:[*_`]{0,2}(?:open|ope[*_`]{0,2}n)[*_`]{0,2}|[*_`]{0,2}(?:settled|set[*_`]{0,2}tled)[*_`]{0,2})[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}New[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Brainstorm|Bra[*_`]{0,2}instorm)[*_`]{0,2}[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*[^|\\\\r\\\\n]*[ \\\\t]*\\\\|[ \\\\t]*(?:[*_`]{0,2}(?:open|ope[*_`]{0,2}n)[*_`]{0,2}|[*_`]{0,2}(?:settled|set[*_`]{0,2}tled)[*_`]{0,2})[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t\\\\r]*$|^[ \\\\t]*\\\\|?[ \\\\t]*[*_`]{0,2}New[*_`]{0,2}[\\\\s*_`]{1,8}[*_`]{0,2}(?:Product|Pro[*_`]{0,2}duct)[*_`]{0,2}[\\