n in Pregnancy, which still carries an unsettled thread, to appear on at least one log line whose last field is open, with a middle field for the Doc stage. Grouping by article is what the leaf does: an article with two open comments satisfies it once, which is the same grouping the summary figure uses. Markdown emphasis, casing, tabs, CRLF and optional outer pipes all pass.\",\n              \"why_justification\": \"The summary says 11 articles are still open. A run that took the row-grain reading counts 15 there, and a run that treated the three settled threads as unsettled counts 14; both leave a review log whose open lines no longer group to the article set these leaves pin. Grouping the log's own rows by article is the only way the per-row deliverable and the summary can be shown to be the same audit.\"\n            },\n            \"source\": {\n              \"type\": \"file\",", "numLines": 717, "startLine": 1, "totalLines": 1302, "truncatedByTokenCap": true}}

